                <pb facs="0302" n="2004" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p2/pg2004"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">774.5/2–2853: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1109<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom (Holmes)
                        to the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-02-28T11:00:00+00:00">February 28, 1953—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4848. Eyes only Secretary. I do not regard following encrypted telegram from
                    Aldrich from RMS <hi rendition="#italic">Queen Elizabeth</hi> regarding US–UK
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ad referendum</hi> agreement on Egypt to be
                    inconsistent with paragraph 1 Embassy’s telegram 4840, February 27: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Eden stated that while Blue Agreement has never been formally approved
                            by Cabinet action HMG in fact desires have it put into effect and
                            desires our full support as indicated to accomplish this.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I believe position to be as follows: (1) There is no Cabinet opposition to
                    agreement per se; but (2) Churchill strongly desires military association with
                    negotiations and, in this situation, Cabinet has not given formal approval to
                    agreement pending resolution this question.</p>
                <p>I feel confident that regardless our decision re military participation, Eden
                    would want proceed with negotiations on basis [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >bases</hi>?] agreement. However, I am sure that you will bear in mind that
                    factors outlined second paragraph Embassy’s telegram 4840 together with
                    Churchill’s upredictability, might create complications, and delay. In long run,
                    however, I think Eden would have his way.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Holmes</hi></hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
